        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-template-v1",
          "portId": "root",
          "name": "Lionel Template v1"
        },
        "title": "Lionel Template v1",
        "purpose": "Model a Lionel episode with reusable class-backed analytical, navigation, media, actor, research, and rhetorical structures.",
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎙️ Lionel Template v1\n\n## Class-backed episode grammar\n\nConfigure the **Episode** first. Then add only the structures the transcript actually needs.\n\n**Episode configuration** → container + sequence controller + navigation mode  \n**Topic Threads** → where the conversation goes  \n**Issue Scopes** → what question each claim or move belongs to  \n**Media Source + Segment** → exactly what outside material is referenced  \n**Lionel Operations** → reusable rhetorical moves  \n**Actor Field / Research Funnel / Coalition** → higher-order analytical structures\n\n> The template provides vocabulary, not a cage.",
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.summary",
          "label": "Lionel Template v1"
        },
        "payload": "node.web.summary",
        "intent": "node",
        "key": "node.web.summary",
        "viewRole": "summary",
        "viewKind": "display",
        "semanticLevel": "summary",
        "visibilityRole": "browser"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-template-v1-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Using Lionel Template v1",
      "position": {
        "x": -160,
        "y": 980
      },
      "width": 820,
      "height": 390,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-template-v1"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# 🧭 Authoring Loop\n\n1. Configure **Lionel Episode**: container, sequence controller, navigation mode.\n2. Replace **Primary Issue** with the episode's actual analytical question. Duplicate Issue Scope only for a truly distinct question.\n3. Use **Topic Thread** for conversational navigation. Keep it separate from Issue Scope.\n4. Duplicate **Lionel Operation** for recurring moves such as issue analysis, analogy, scenario simulation, media commentary, perspective-taking, actor mapping, and synthesis.\n5. Add **Media Source** and **Timed Media Segment** only when outside media matters. Keep source and commentary ranges distinct.\n6. Keep **Actor Field**, **Research Funnel**, and **Coalition** only when the transcript supports them.\n7. Re-evaluate every starter semantic edge. Delete any edge that is not true in the derived episode.\n\n**Attribution rule:** transcript claims remain attributed claims. Structural observations are not evidence that the claims are true.\n\nSee `SKILL.md` for the full derivation contract."
        }
      }
    },
